act \nAction Chunking with Transformers (ACT)⟨44⟩ is an imitation-learning method that predicts short action chunks instead of single steps. It learns from teleoperated data and often achieves high success rates.\nThis policy has been trained and pushed to the Hub using LeRobot⟨45⟩. See the full documentation at LeRobot Docs⟨46⟩.\n* * *\n##   ⟨40⟩ How to Get Started with the Model \nFor a complete walkthrough, see the training guide⟨47⟩. Below is the short version on how to train and run inference/eval:\n###   ⟨41⟩ Train from scratch \n\n```\nlerobot-train \\\n  --dataset.repo_id=${HF_USER}/<dataset> \\\n  --policy.type=act \\\n  --output_dir=outputs/train/<desired_policy_repo_id> \\\n  --job_name=lerobot_training \\\n  --policy.device=cuda \\\n  --policy.repo_id=${HF_USER}/<desired_policy_repo_id>\n  --wandb.enable=true\n\n```\n\n_Writes checkpoints to`outputs/train/<desired_policy_repo_id>/checkpoints/`._\n###   ⟨42⟩ Evaluate the policy/run inference \n\n```\nlerobot-record \\\n  --robot.type=so100_follower \\\n  --dataset.repo_id=<hf_user>/eval_<dataset> \\\n  --policy.path=<hf_user>/<desired_policy_repo_id> \\\n  --episodes=10\n\n```\n\nPrefix the dataset repo with **eval_** and supply `--policy.path` pointing to a local or hub checkpoint.\n* * *\n##   ⟨43⟩ Model Details \n  * **License:** apache-2.0\n\n\n\nDownloads last month\n    37\nSafetensors⟨48⟩\nModel size\n51.7M params\nTensor type\nF32 \n·\nFiles info\nVideo Preview\nRobotics\nloading\n##  Dataset used to train coport-uni/FR5_task3_turn_the_sliver_air_valve_90_degress_counterclockwise_200_act_h200_model\n#### coport-uni/FR5_task3_turn_the_sliver_air_valve_90_degress_counterclockwise_200 Viewer • Updated 23 days ago • 145k • 246 ⟨49⟩\n##  Paper for coport-uni/FR5_task3_turn_the_sliver_air_valve_90_degress_counterclockwise_200_act_h200_model\n#### Learning Fine-Grained Bimanual Manipulation with Low-Cost Hardware Paper • 2304.13705 • Published Apr 23, 2023 • 7 ⟨44⟩\nSystem theme\nCompany\nTOS⟨50⟩ Privacy